{"name":"Phantom Ship","hex":"#2f3434","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"phantom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ghost or apparition.","Something apparently seen, heard, or sensed, but having no physical reality; an image that appears only in the mind; an illusion or delusion."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Illusive.","Fictitious or nonexistent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phantom"},{"term":"ship","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A water-borne vessel generally larger than a boat.","A vessel which travels through any medium other than across land, such as an airship or spaceship."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To send by water-borne transport.","To send (a parcel or container) to a recipient (by any means of transport)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ship"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghost ship","blocks":[{"text":"A ghost ship, also known as a phantom ship, is a vessel with no living crew aboard; it may be a fictional ghostly vessel, such as the Flying Dutchman, or a physical derelict found adrift with its crew missing or dead, like the Mary Celeste. The term is sometimes used for ships that have been decommissioned but not yet scrapped, as well as drifting boats that have been found after breaking loose of their ropes and being carried away by the wind or the waves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Deering2.jpg/330px-Deering2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_ship","wikidata":"Q281019"},{"title":"Phantom Ship (island)","blocks":[{"text":"Phantom Ship is a small island in Crater Lake in the U.S. state of Oregon. It is a natural rock formation pillar which derives its name from its resemblance to a ghost ship, especially in foggy and low-light conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Phantom_Ship_-_Crater_Lake_National_Park_%2815176204199%29.jpg/330px-Phantom_Ship_-_Crater_Lake_National_Park_%2815176204199%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantom_Ship_(island)","wikidata":"Q7180593"},{"title":"Ship","blocks":[{"text":"A ship is a large watercraft designed for travel across the surface of a body of water, carrying cargo or passengers, or in support of specialized tasks such as warfare, oceanography and fishing. Ships are generally distinguished from boats, based on size, shape, load capacity and purpose. Ships have supported exploration, trade, warfare, migration, colonization, and science. Ship transport is responsible for the largest portion of world commerce."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg/330px-Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship","wikidata":"Q11446"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg/500px-Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg/500px-Flying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Flying Dutchman by Albert Pinkham Ryder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlying_Dutchman%2C_the.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Epave_Marlborough.JPG/500px-Epave_Marlborough.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Epave_Marlborough.JPG/500px-Epave_Marlborough.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse